# Cusimanse project instructions

The Markdown contract defines the research question, authorization, scope and acceptance criteria. The experiment YAML defines research requirements and policy; do not embed infrastructure implementation in it.

Use Goose as the reference primary operator. The selected agent is allowed to resolve and operate registered capabilities through `cmd/cusimanse`.

Use `go run ./cmd/cusimanse resolve <experiment>` before execution. After explicit researcher approval for approval-gated actions, use `go run ./cmd/cusimanse --approved run <experiment>`.

Never create trusted profiles, mutate infrastructure recipes, expand policy scope, or execute untrusted workloads on the host. Start declared guest instrumentation before workloads and preserve evidence/provenance before VM destruction.

Use project Skills and specialist subagents for focused analysis. Keep independent verification separate from primary analysis. Do not introduce a second orchestration controller.

Raw runtime artifacts are evidence. Model output is analysis only. Provider credentials remain outside Git.
